WEBVTT

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:38.320
The Hollywood movie <i>Interview with a 
Vampire</i> was released in fall of 1994.

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:42.390
As I was a growing girl at the time,

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:46.750
it would not be an exaggeration to say 
that this movie shaped my personality

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:49.770
and became the foundation of my interests.

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:54.240
Lead actor Brad Pitt does an 
impressive job portraying Louis,

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:59.390
a man who struggles with being a vampire 
due to his lingering human conscience.

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:02.020
Achieving an unexpectedly delicate sexiness

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:05.320
and covering up his crude 
acting with his good looks,

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:09.820
Tom Cruise, who plays Lestat, 
undoubtedly gained new fans.

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:12.320
The supporting cast were handsome, as well,

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:16.220
and the casting was as thorough as 
you'd expect from a Hollywood movie.

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:18.480
...Is what I'd like to say,

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:21.340
but the critical role of Daniel 
the interviewer is played

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:24.610
by the slightly uninspiring 
Christian Slater.

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:28.240
He performance is hardly bad, but it's 
a little rough around the edges.

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:32.750
He was good as the apprentice 
monk in <i>The Name of the Rose</i>,

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:34.600
but he's been lackluster ever since.

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:38.900
If River Phoenix had been 
cast as originally planned,

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:43.590
I personally would have found it 
to be an even more enjoyable film.

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:49.180
But the interactions between beautiful 
men and confessions of love

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:52.020
lured not only fans of 
homosexual and BL content,

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:56.950
but also many fujoshi into its 
gorgeous and aesthetic world.

00:02:57.550 --> 00:03:02.750
The original novel by Anne 
Rice is a cult classic.

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:05.040
The world depicted is so similar 
to that of <i>Poe no Ichizoku</i>

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:06.920
that it could be considered a 
live-action version of the series.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:11.180
Its themes can be summed up as the 
sorrow and suffering of vampires.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:15.910
Despite all his agonizing, 
Louis ends up as an empty vampire.

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:21.560
The delicious final scene ends with 
a revived Lestat's triumphant smile.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:25.080
It's fine, though, since it's entertaining.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:28.130
The director would be to blame if he 
failed to produce an entertaining film

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:30.090
with such an extravagant cast.

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:34.360
The girl who played Claudia 
wasn't very cute.

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:35.500
You think so?

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:39.010
I think it's better that she wasn't 
played by a beautiful girl.

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:40.480
Why is that?

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:43.250
Because this is a movie about handsome men.

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:46.260
The women and girls can 
simply be women and girls.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:47.480
Are you sure?

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:51.030
Besides, I thought her 
acting was impressive.

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:54.950
She has the mind of an adult, but her 
body is forever that of a child's.

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:57.500
The suffering and frustration 
she portrayed felt so real.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:58.740
By the end of the movie,

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:01.640
she was making the kinds of expressions 
you'd expect from a middle-aged woman.

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:05.500
I imagine male fans were disappointed.

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:06.480
You're right.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:11.330
Hetero men feel like they've wasted their time 
if they didn't get to look at beautiful women.

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:14.540
<i>Now that you mention it, you might be right.</i>

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:18.010
<i>What type of beautiful girls 
do hetero dudes like, anyway?</i>

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:20.370
An interview.

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:21.090
That's right.

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:21.950
With Mai?

00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:22.600
Yeah.

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:26.370
I want to film it and make a documentary.

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:29.610
What are you talking about? 
We can't do that.

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:32.710
You'd be exposing Mai's secret to the world.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:35.220
And besides, we've got to 
respect Mai's privacy.

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:38.880
She doesn't have to answer any questions 
she doesn't want to answer.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:43.460
You're lying. I know exactly what 
you're up to since you chose Mai.

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:48.020
You'd be exposing the Blood Donation Club's 
impure blood donation activities, too.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:51.250
What if Mai gets kicked 
out of this high school?

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:57.020
Just because it's called a documentary 
doesn't mean everything depicted is real.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:59.310
As a film, it's necessarily a fabrication.

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:02.740
In other words, it doesn't 
work without direction.

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:06.360
You mean you'll exaggerate 
Mai's secret, right?

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:12.120
I'll censor her eyes with a bar 
and call her "Vampire Girl A."

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:17.180
In what universe is there an 
anonymous "Vampire Girl A?"

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:18.900
That's what makes it interesting.

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:22.700
I won't be interviewing 
some commonplace girl.

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:26.450
You just don't understand. 
This is why I can't stand amateurs.

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:28.220
And I don't care to understand.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:32.660
I don't need you making waves in 
my happy little life with Mai.

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:35.560
Happy little life, huh?

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:36.500
What's wrong with that?

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:39.410
Nothing, if you're happy with that.

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:42.940
But normally, I'd imagine 
people would be more curious.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:45.940
Curious about what?

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:48.420
Oh, sorry.

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:52.940
I meant Mai's personal history. Her past.

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:57.540
I was just wondering what 
you even know about Mai.

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:00.980
Well, if you're not concerned 
about the true identity

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:03.560
of the friend you're living 
with under the same roof,

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:05.930
I suppose that could be considered 
magnanimous or cool.

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:10.090
Mai's past doesn't bother—

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:12.880
It doesn't bother you, except for Franken.

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:13.260
What?

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:16.010
And if you're happy now, 
then none of it matters.

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:21.410
I'm giving up on the idea. 
You should forget about it, too.

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:24.280
Huh? Wha— Maki, wait!

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:36.890
<i>In order to minimize information leaks,</i>

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:40.800
<i>on the condition that even our blood 
brothers and sisters would be excluded,</i>

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:45.390
<i>I agreed to help Maki make her movie.</i>

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:47.390
Good grief.

00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:49.550
I thought I'd be able to go home early tonight

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:51.490
and enjoy some sake while viewing the moon.

00:06:51.490 --> 00:06:57.260
You say that, but you're itching to 
use that clapperboard you're holding.

00:06:57.260 --> 00:06:59.000
As the instructor in charge,

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:02.970
I can't allow you to perform 
extracurricular activities without me.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:09.030
You're lucky you have such 
an understanding teacher.

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:11.650
Mai, are you okay?

00:07:11.650 --> 00:07:14.920
If you decide you don't want to 
do this, we can stop anytime.

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:17.080
And you don't have to answer any 
questions you don't want to—

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:19.540
Hey, stay out of this.

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:23.000
I'm okay. I'm actually kind of excited.

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:31.170
Ready, action!

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:37.100
M-san, let's dive right in.

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:39.270
What's your favorite blood type?

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:43.410
I don't have one. I was taught 
not to be a picky eater.

00:07:43.410 --> 00:07:46.380
Do you prefer men's blood or women's blood?

00:07:46.830 --> 00:07:50.620
I actually prefer men's blood.

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:53.480
But I'd never ask for it. 
Not until we win the war!

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:57.590
I see. You prefer the blood 
of boys. Why is that?

00:07:57.590 --> 00:08:00.220
It's kind of thick.

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:03.820
It has an animal-like smell 
that whets my appetite.

00:08:03.820 --> 00:08:08.210
Then you must find the blood 
of timid boys disappointing.

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:09.670
I do.

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:13.770
If I'm allowed to choose, I prefer 
the blood of aggressive men.

00:08:13.770 --> 00:08:16.200
But I'd never ask for it. 
Not until we win the war!

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:19.660
You're such a good-natured vampire, Mai-san.

00:08:20.230 --> 00:08:24.020
Have you always been such a kind person?

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:26.850
I'm not so sure.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:30.050
I'm sure you had lots of friends.

00:08:30.050 --> 00:08:34.100
It was a long, long time ago. 
I don't remember very well.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:36.770
What's your greatest childhood memory?

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:39.740
I forgot.

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:42.000
Cut!

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:44.550
Doctor, I'm the director!

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:47.080
Our food has arrived.

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:49.730
Thanks again.

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:57.120
It seems like she doesn't 
want to talk about her past.

00:08:57.540 --> 00:08:59.870
Perhaps she has a secret.

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:01.530
A secret?

00:09:01.530 --> 00:09:03.710
Yeah, maybe.

00:09:03.710 --> 00:09:09.090
There's a reason Mai's too 
timid to bite people?

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:13.060
Maybe she experienced some 
kind of trauma as a child.

00:09:13.060 --> 00:09:15.120
You guys are overthinking it.

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:17.530
Mai's simply a pure girl.

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:19.590
You're green.

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:22.740
Green like the Jolly Green Giant.

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:26.710
Not only is that an old reference, 
but it's kind of obscure.

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:29.620
I kind of like his peas.

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:35.620
I'm starting to feel sleepy...

00:09:41.780 --> 00:09:43.510
Huh? Mai?

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:48.540
You bitch, you drugged her, didn't you?

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:53.100
I just mixed in a tiny bit of blood 
containing a sleep inducing agent.

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:54.690
What?!

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:57.000
Don't worry. It has no side effects.

00:09:57.300 --> 00:09:59.160
Doctor, did you—

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:02.250
I'm a public health doctor with no morals.

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:04.100
Hypnotherapy...

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:09.090
That lukewarm interview style you were 
using earlier will never get us anywhere.

00:10:09.090 --> 00:10:12.120
How could you do this without Mai's consent?

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:15.640
As an orthodox documentary maker, 
I have some doubts about this.

00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:19.110
That's exactly what makes you lukewarm.

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:20.150
Like the Jolly Green Giant's thawed—

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:21.060
I like his peas.

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:24.110
For the record, I'm against this.

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:31.200
Mitsugu, are you sure you're not 
scared to learn about Mai's past?

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:36.740
I'll take your silence as consent.

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:39.030
Let's continue the interview.

00:10:48.520 --> 00:10:52.490
Since you set this in motion, 
let me tell you one thing.

00:10:53.080 --> 00:10:57.460
There are some things in this world 
that you're better off not knowing.

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:00.620
Let's get started.

00:11:01.250 --> 00:11:03.650
Ready, action!

00:11:08.190 --> 00:11:12.540
You are currently descending some stairs.

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:14.970
One step.

00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:17.270
Two steps.

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:19.530
Three steps.

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:22.180
Your foot slipped.

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:24.310
Doctor!

00:11:24.310 --> 00:11:26.910
This isn't the time for jokes!

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:28.240
You slipped on the third step

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:31.240
but immediately regained your 
balance and stepped down...

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:33.370
...onto the final step.

00:11:38.990 --> 00:11:46.880
When you open the door in front of 
you, you see yourself as a child.

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:55.570
Where are you now?

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:02.320
Inside a carriage. It's moving.

00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:05.550
Where is it traveling?

00:12:06.070 --> 00:12:11.250
A dark road. The scenery 
outside is a blazing red.

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:13.450
Who are you with?

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:15.110
My Daddy, and...

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:18.200
Oh, this brings back memories.

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:21.570
It's my real mother who gave birth to me.

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:24.400
Mother!

00:12:24.750 --> 00:12:27.690
It's all right, Mai. Father 
will take care of it.

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:32.430
Mai, I promise I'll protect you two.

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:36.050
But it's so red outside!

00:12:36.050 --> 00:12:38.020
That's the evening sun.

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:42.810
But I see so many black crosses!

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:45.560
Those are the shadows of trees.

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:49.470
I hear horrible groans and screams!

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:52.840
Those are the crows cawing.

00:12:52.840 --> 00:12:56.100
But I smell flesh burning!

00:12:56.100 --> 00:13:01.340
Mai, you mustn't look at, 
listen to or smell anything.

00:13:04.070 --> 00:13:08.940
Decades pass. Where are you now?

00:13:10.590 --> 00:13:16.220
I'm traveling from town to 
town across unfamiliar lands.

00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:20.830
Where are your father and mother?

00:13:21.350 --> 00:13:22.870
Mother...

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:24.510
Where is mother?

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:26.430
Where is mother?!

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:33.540
Mother!

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:37.030
Mai, run! Run away!

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:41.950
Run, Mai! Forget about Mom! Just run!

00:13:42.770 --> 00:13:45.300
No! No!

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:48.110
Mother!

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:50.900
No! No!

00:13:50.900 --> 00:13:53.930
Mother!

00:13:57.110 --> 00:13:58.920
They slaughtered her.

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:02.760
It was a witch hunt. Poor woman.

00:14:05.270 --> 00:14:06.670
Mai...

00:14:06.670 --> 00:14:10.230
Those who hunt humans are 
in turn hunted by humans.

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:15.050
Such is the fate of those 
who drink human blood.

00:14:15.050 --> 00:14:18.150
Let's stop. Let's not do this anymore.

00:14:18.150 --> 00:14:19.950
Who cares about any of that?

00:14:21.650 --> 00:14:22.770
Mitsugu.

00:14:23.270 --> 00:14:27.720
Are you sure you're not afraid 
to face the true Mai?

00:14:27.980 --> 00:14:31.980
I just don't want to make 
Mai suffer anymore!

00:14:31.980 --> 00:14:32.860
You're wrong.

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:41.820
You're afraid to know what truth is 
hidden behind Mai's pretty little face.

00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:47.110
Well, Mitsugu Bambam. 
Should we continue or not?

00:14:47.460 --> 00:14:50.300
As interested party number one, you decide.

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:52.930
My name isn't Mitsugu Bambam.

00:14:53.350 --> 00:14:54.930
It's Mitsugu Bamba.

00:14:56.810 --> 00:15:01.880
More time passes. Where are you now?

00:15:02.610 --> 00:15:04.250
I...

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:17.830
My Daddy and I left Europe.

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:20.780
We're heading to the New World.

00:15:20.780 --> 00:15:24.210
More time passes.

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:29.380
It's different from Europe 
and its tired traditions.

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:35.970
The city was filled with people of different 
races speaking different languages.

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:43.510
We hid among the crowds 
and continued our journey.

00:15:43.970 --> 00:15:46.930
More time passes.

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:50.810
Where are you?

00:15:50.810 --> 00:15:53.740
We're near a river called the Mississippi.

00:15:54.150 --> 00:15:56.730
We live on a large plantation.

00:15:57.160 --> 00:16:01.330
We're surrounded by dark-skinned 
nannies and servants.

00:16:01.330 --> 00:16:03.990
Sounds straight out of <i>Gone with the Wind</i>.

00:16:03.990 --> 00:16:06.240
Gone with the what now?

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:08.160
Just die, you ignorant savage!

00:16:08.160 --> 00:16:10.370
Based on a novel by Margaret Mitchell,

00:16:10.370 --> 00:16:14.950
produced by David O. Selznick, 
and directed by Victor Fleming.

00:16:16.180 --> 00:16:19.000
Vivien Leigh and Clark Gable.

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:23.070
Leslie Howard, Olivia de 
Havilland, and Thomas Mitchell.

00:16:23.070 --> 00:16:24.500
Who?

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:29.240
You've never heard of the masterpiece 
that won nine Academy Awards?

00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:32.350
Oh, that long-ass movie.

00:16:32.350 --> 00:16:34.310
I've seen a bit of it on TV.

00:16:34.310 --> 00:16:37.290
The Keiko Toda and Toru Emori dub?

00:16:37.290 --> 00:16:39.980
I forgot. Actually, I never remembered.

00:16:39.980 --> 00:16:44.950
By the way, the Warner Brothers dub 
featured Akio Otsuka as Rhett Butler.

00:16:44.950 --> 00:16:49.970
Scarlett O'hara's sister Suellen 
O'Hara was voiced by Atsuko Tanaka.

00:16:49.970 --> 00:16:51.610
So, what?

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:57.420
On that plantation, I met my first friends.

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:03.450
Starting today, this girl 
will be your friend.

00:17:03.450 --> 00:17:05.400
Her name is Caroline Irene.

00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:08.860
Call her Carreen.

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:14.260
Carreen came from an orphanage.

00:17:15.900 --> 00:17:20.370
We quickly became friends.

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:25.220
We were like sisters.

00:17:25.590 --> 00:17:27.920
It really is <i>Gone with the Wind</i>.

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:31.630
Carreen, also known as 
Caroline Irene O'Hara is—

00:17:31.630 --> 00:17:33.350
What happened next?

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:35.950
One day...

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:43.840
Mai, it's about time you began to 
prepare to become independent vampire.

00:17:43.840 --> 00:17:45.330
Independent?

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:52.140
That's right. A fully-fledged 
vampire must hunt their own prey.

00:17:52.140 --> 00:17:53.450
Prey?

00:17:53.450 --> 00:18:00.080
You must sink your own fangs into your prey, 
drink its blood, and control your prey.

00:18:00.570 --> 00:18:04.100
Naturally, you won't be able 
to do that right away.

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:07.590
You'll need a partner to practice 
on in order to get used to it.

00:18:08.530 --> 00:18:12.650
Take a look. That's your first prey.

00:18:14.040 --> 00:18:19.790
Carreen had been brought to the 
plantation for that purpose.

00:18:20.730 --> 00:18:25.420
I see. It's like how raptors will 
offer live prey to their chicks.

00:18:25.420 --> 00:18:26.450
Ugh!

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:28.580
Cut the old-fashioned reactions.

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:31.610
He offered a live human to his own child.

00:18:31.610 --> 00:18:34.200
Vampire parents are incredible.

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:36.670
What happened next?

00:18:37.190 --> 00:18:40.600
Naturally, I rejected the idea.

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:44.650
I couldn't drink the blood 
of my precious friend.

00:18:44.650 --> 00:18:46.870
Of course not.

00:18:46.870 --> 00:18:48.100
And then?

00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:52.630
Daddy became angry. 
He exposed me to the sun—

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:56.080
No, he forced me to fast.

00:18:56.950 --> 00:18:58.730
Fast?

00:18:58.730 --> 00:19:05.300
Pure-blooded vampires raise their children 
by allowing them to drink blood from their arm.

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:11.660
After I lost my mother, I was 
raised on my Daddy's blood.

00:19:13.060 --> 00:19:19.190
He did it so she could become 
independent and leave the nest.

00:19:20.060 --> 00:19:22.790
It's standard practice in the natural world.

00:19:22.790 --> 00:19:25.710
If anything, humans are the exception.

00:19:25.710 --> 00:19:28.310
Like a fox driving off her kits.

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:30.340
And then?

00:19:30.340 --> 00:19:33.530
I dried up.

00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:37.930
I'd never experienced anything 
like it in my life.

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:40.260
I felt so dry.

00:19:40.590 --> 00:19:43.160
My hunger tore me apart.

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:49.390
No matter how much I screamed and cried, 
Daddy wouldn't offer me his arm.

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:54.800
For three days and nights, I suffered 
and cried until I couldn't anymore.

00:19:59.100 --> 00:20:03.300
Then that night arrived.

00:20:12.990 --> 00:20:16.390
I snuck into her room.

00:20:17.290 --> 00:20:21.700
I stood beside her as she slept peacefully.

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:37.840
No!

00:20:42.610 --> 00:20:45.750
I feel so dizzy in the morning.

00:20:46.340 --> 00:20:49.420
Everyone knows what I'm thinking.

00:20:49.880 --> 00:20:53.110
My stomach is so excited.

00:20:53.380 --> 00:20:56.590
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:20:57.010 --> 00:21:04.260
The night is anxious, 
your sleepiness will go flying.

00:21:04.260 --> 00:21:10.740
Blood vessels flow so 
smoothly, not enough blood...

00:21:04.470 --> 00:21:09.290
So, what are you going to 
do with the video you shot?

00:21:09.290 --> 00:21:10.740
What? Maki...

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:16.160
After the story she told us, 
I can't release it to the public.

00:21:17.320 --> 00:21:20.500
If I'm empathizing with my subject,

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:24.740
then I still have a lot to learn 
as a documentary director.

00:21:24.990 --> 00:21:30.970
It may be the fate of vampires, 
but it's a sad thing.

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:32.760
No, it's not.

00:21:32.760 --> 00:21:34.890
What's not sad?

00:21:35.230 --> 00:21:37.310
Mai isn't alone anymore.

00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:39.260
She has me...

00:21:39.750 --> 00:21:42.270
...and her blood brothers and 
sisters from the night school.

00:21:58.770 --> 00:22:04.410
Someday Mai may drink your blood.

00:22:05.190 --> 00:22:08.960
I hope you're prepared for that.
